        caller verification, and cleanup verification.
  - [ ] Diagnostics, stable returns, and rejection of bare callbacks.
- [ ] Require each command fixture to declare its gate, execution, intrinsic,
      timeout, retry-safety, cleanup, and expected evidence observations.
- [ ] Keep domain command suites focused on normalization, target resolution,
      native action receipt, readback, cleanup receipt, and diagnostic
      projection rather than duplicating runner mechanics.
- [ ] Run the complete command-engine and directly affected service/protocol
      suites.
- [ ] Perform a follow-up qualification review against every bullet in the
      proposal's command-engine qualification section.

Completion criteria:

- [ ] Reusable suites prove common lifecycle behavior once and can qualify each
      migrated definition with a small fixture.
- [ ] Structured command and cleanup evidence is complete, bounded, and
      ancestry-valid.

