- [ ] Require every live run used as acceptance evidence to reach a terminal
      report and include cleanup confirmation; treat silent timeout or external
      interruption as inconclusive.
- [ ] Compare source, installed, and packaged behavior and declarations.
- [ ] Validate active and retained service reads plus persisted results expose
      complete, equal service-run, suite-execution, and test-attempt cleanup
      transaction sets.
- [ ] Audit every public command against the phase-1 migration inventory.
- [ ] Audit every acceptance criterion in
      `docs/verified-command-execution-proposal.md` against implementation and
      concrete evidence.
- [ ] Audit proposal-to-plan coverage in both directions and record any explicit
      deferral with rationale rather than silently accepting a gap.
- [ ] Perform the required follow-up implementation review after final fixes and
      before marking the plan complete.
- [ ] Run `git diff --check` and inspect the final worktree for unintended or
      unrelated changes.

Completion criteria:

- [ ] Every declared public command routes through the common runner and every
      proposal acceptance criterion has implementation plus proportionate
      evidence.
- [ ] Command failures reach Busted with exact stage attribution; command
      success reflects the strongest truthful intrinsic guarantee and optional
      caller postcondition.
- [ ] `ONCE`, explicit retry-safe execution, workflows, effect-driven claims,
      verified cleanup, owner-scoped journals/results, and quarantine behavior
      pass their final qualification.
- [ ] The complete source, installed, packaged, framework, service, and bounded
      live contracts agree.

## Final acceptance

- [ ] Every requirement in `docs/verified-command-execution-proposal.md` is
      implemented or explicitly deferred with an approved rationale.
- [ ] The standalone DAG prerequisite is complete under its own `.todo`.
- [ ] Every built-in and project command uses the one verified-command runner.
- [ ] Every command has a finite effective deadline, explicit preflight,
      declared primary policy, and truthful intrinsic evidence.
- [ ] Caller verification remains optional and cannot weaken intrinsic proof.
- [ ] Every active resource claim belongs to one confirmed effect and one
      cleanup transaction.
- [ ] Every retained transaction has exactly one terminal disposition in its
      authoritative journal and owner-specific result projection.
- [ ] Cleanup restoration, verification, retry, dependency planning, reporting,
      and executor quarantine satisfy the approved contracts at service, suite,
      test, and command lifetimes.
- [ ] No legacy adapter, duplicate facade implementation, unlimited timeout, or
      parallel cleanup/resource/result ledger remains.
- [ ] Required tests, declarations, documentation, packaging, persistence, and
      terminal live evidence are complete.
